#: data/io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia.metainfo.xml.in:11
msgid ""
"Groovia is a local music player for GNOME that makes a personal collection "
"feel like a record shelf. It scans folders in the background, groups tracks "
"into albums, reads embedded metadata and artwork, and keeps the library in a "
"local database."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia.metainfo.xml.in:12
msgid ""
"The player combines GStreamer playback with an animated vinyl deck, a "
"responsive queue, configurable crossfade, gapless playback, ReplayGain "
"normalization, notifications, and MPRIS controls where supported. Album "
"artwork can shape the interface's color palette, while animations and other "
"visual options can be adjusted in Preferences."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia.metainfo.xml.in:13
msgid ""
"Organize music with playlists and favorites, search and sort tracks, create "
"custom playlist covers, and play common local formats including MP3, FLAC, "
"Ogg Vorbis, Opus, WAV, AAC, and M4A."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia.metainfo.xml.in:14
msgid ""
"Optional Spotify imports use spotDL to find matching audio and preserve "
"playlist metadata and artwork. Groovia does not stream or download audio "
"directly from Spotify. Synchronized and plain lyrics can be imported, "
"downloaded when supported, edited locally, and displayed line by line or "
"word by word."
msgstr ""

#: data/io.github.Lluciocc.Groovia.metainfo.xml.in:15
msgid ""
"Auto DJ is an opt-in feature that analyzes tracks in the background and "
"plans queue-safe transitions using phrase, silence, beat, tempo, and bass "
"information when available. It keeps the queue intact and falls back "
"gracefully when advanced audio processing is unavailable."
msgstr ""

